Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||03:20 PM||||I like the way it looks. We need to have more fieros in non-stock colors. Has purple finally lost its connotation for a car? For quite a while purple cars were mostly owned by people of a certain 'orientiation', to the point that most car manufactures stopped painting cars purple, cause most people wouldnt buy them anymore.<P>But I did hear recently that some cars are now available in purple again.<P>I have a slight problem with this on my hobie cat sailboat. It was made in '81 and the sails look like a giant rainbow. i have been approached by guys several times while setting up my hobie at marinas, who thought the rainbow sails were a 'statement' on my behalf. I dont really mind, its not like its a problem, I simply tell them thats the way the boat was made 20 years ago and no - Im not gay (not that theres anything wrong with that).<P> I am still undecided on the color I want to paint my 85 SE - Im leaning towards a pure blue, or maybe ultramarine blue. The purple looks great though, i like it.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||sqoach||05-14-2001||04:05 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B> I am still undecided on the color I want to paint my 85 SE - Im leaning towards a pure blue, or maybe ultramarine blue. The purple looks great though, i like it.<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, there's a guy here in town that has an early 80s ultramarine blue Olds Cutlass. And it's not you're everyday cutlass. It's shaved everywhere. Remote open doors, trunk, the works. Has a big cowl scoop on the hood. It's lowered and has 16 wheels. And has a HUGE stereo system. Like 16 speakers! It's pretty slick, but not my taste really.<P>Oh yeah, forgot to mention he recently put ghost flames on it. At certain angles and light, they look pink!<P>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 05-14-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
